        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Ff142 Integrity-Policy]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27530</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27530"/>
        <updated>2025-08-08T02:06:41.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF142 adds support for <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Integrity-Policy" rel="nofollow">Integrity-Policy</a> and <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Integrity-Policy-Report-Only" rel="nofollow">Integrity-Policy-Report-Only</a> on nightly in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1976656" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1976656</a> [behind pref <code class="notranslate">security.integrity_policy.enabled</code> enabled in nightly).</p>
<p dir="auto">The bug actually just mentions the non-report version, but you wouldn't do one without the other (<a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1976656#c10" rel="nofollow">seeking confirmation in issue</a></p>
<p dir="auto">This just adds preview to both features.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3302143499" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40667" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/40667/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40667">mdn/content#40667</a></p>]]></content>
